# Agent Web Search Skill for Coding Agents

## Overview

The **agent-web-search** package provides two powerful command-line utilities for web search and content fetching:

| Tool | Purpose | Main modes |
|------|---------|-----------|
| **brave-search** | Privacy-focused web search using Brave's independent search index | `brave-search "<query>" -n <N> [--json]` |
| **linkup-search** | AI-specific agentic search with deep research capability | `linkup-search search "<query>" -n <N> [--json]`<br>`linkup-search fetch "<url>" [--json]` |

Both tools output **machine-readable JSON** for coding agents and human-readable formatted text by default.

---

## 1. Prerequisites & Installation

### Requirement: `uv`

The **agent-web-search** package relies on `uv` for dependency management and execution. If `uv` is not installed, install it first:

```bash
# Install uv (one-time setup)
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
```

### Installing agent-web-search

#### Option A: Install from GitHub (recommended for latest version)
```bash
# Install directly from the main branch
uv tool install "git+https://github.com/uv-genai/agent-web-search.git"

# Or install a specific version
uv tool install "git+https://github.com/uv-genai/agent-web-search.git@v2.0.0"
```

#### Option B: Clone and install locally
```bash
git clone https://github.com/uv-genai/agent-web-search.git
cd agent-web-search
uv sync
```

After installation, the following commands will be available on your `$PATH`:
- `brave-search`
- `linkup-search`

Verify installation:
```bash
brave-search --help
linkup-search --help
```

### Setting Up API Keys

Before using the tools, you need API keys:

```bash
# Get Brave Search API key from https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/
export BRAVE_API_KEY="your-brave-api-key-here"

# Get Linkup API key from https://app.linkup.so/
export LINKUP_API_KEY="your-linkup-api-key-here"
```

Or create a `.env` file in your project:
```bash
cp /path/to/agent-web-search/.env.example .env
# Edit .env with your API keys
```

