## 3. Linkup Search Tool (`linkup-search`)

### Search Mode

#### Command
```bash
linkup-search search "<query>" [-n <N>] [--depth <depth>] [--output-type <type>] [--json]
```

* `<query>` – the search string (quotes required if it contains spaces)
* `-n <N>` – number of results to return (default: 10, max: 100)
* `--depth <depth>` – search depth: `standard` (fast) or `deep` (thorough, default: standard)
* `--output-type <type>` – output type: `searchResults`, `sourcedAnswer`, or `structured` (default: searchResults)
* `--json` – output raw JSON instead of formatted text
* `--from-date <YYYY-MM-DD>` – filter results from date (optional)
* `--to-date <YYYY-MM-DD>` – filter results to date (optional)
* `--include-domains <domain1> [domain2 ...]` – restrict to specific domains (optional)
* `--exclude-domains <domain1> [domain2 ...]` – exclude specific domains (optional)

### Search JSON output schema (searchResults)
```json
{
  "mode": "search",
  "query": "string",
  "parameters": {
    "num_results_requested": int,
    "depth": "string",
    "output_type": "string"
  },
  "results": [
    {
      "name": "string",
      "url": "string",
      "content": "string",
      "type": "source"
    },
    ...
  ],
  "total_found": int,
  "error": false
}
```

### Example
